        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing, and one answer has to be chosen. Choose the answer the documents support better.\n\nQuestion: Which sports team does White Agwuocha represent or represent?\n\nAnswer A: Bradford City A.F.C.\n  about: White Agwuocha\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"White Agwuocha is a professional footballer who currently plays for Bradford City A.F.C. in the English Football League.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Kristiansund BK\n  about: White Agwuocha\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"White Agwuocha is a professional football player who currently plays for Kristiansund BK, an association football club based in Kristiansund, Norway.\" [document 2]\n\nThe documents:\nDocument 1: White Agwuocha\n\nWhite Agwuocha is a professional footballer who currently plays for Bradford City A.F.C. in the English Football League. Early Life and Career\n\nWhite Agwuocha was born on February 12, 1995, in Lagos, Nigeria. He began his football career at a young age, playing for local clubs in his hometown before moving to England to pursue a professional career. Club Career\n\nAgwuocha joined Bradford City A.F.C. in 2018, signing a three-year contract with the club. Since his debut, he has made over 50 appearances for the team, scoring 12 goals and providing 7 assists. In the 2020-21 season, Agwuocha played a crucial role in Bradford City's promotion to League One, scoring the winning goal in the playoff final against Newport County. Studies and References\n\nA study published in the Journal of Sports Science and Medicine in 2020 analyzed Agwuocha's performance data and found that he was one of the top-performing players in League Two, with a goal-scoring rate of 0.35 goals per 90 minutes. [1]\n\nIn an interview with the Bradford Telegraph and Argus, Agwuocha credited his success to the support of his teammates and the guidance of Bradford City's manager, Stuart McCall. [2]\n\nA report by the English Football League in 2020 highlighted Agwuocha's contributions to Bradford City's promotion campaign, noting that he was one of the team's most consistent performers throughout the season. [3]\n\nReferences\n\n[1] \"Performance Analysis of White Agwuocha in League Two\" by J. Smith et al., Journal of Sports Science and Medicine, Vol. 23, No. 2, 2020. [2] \"White Agwuocha: The Nigerian Sensation Leading Bradford City's Promotion Charge\" by M. Johnson, Bradford Telegraph and Argus, April 15, 2020. [3] \"Bradford City A.F.C. Season Review 2019-20\" by the English Football League, May 2020.\nDocument 2: **White Agwuocha**\n\nWhite Agwuocha is a professional football player who currently plays for Kristiansund BK, an association football club based in Kristiansund, Norway. **Early Life and Career**\n\nThere is limited information available on Agwuocha's early life and career. However, it is known that he has been an active player in the football scene for several years. **Club Career**\n\nAgwuocha's most notable achievement is his current stint with Kristiansund BK, a Norwegian football club that competes in the Eliteserien, the top division of Norwegian football. According to the club's official website, Agwuocha is a member of the first team and has been featured in several matches. [1]\n\n**Evidence of Playing for Kristiansund BK**\n\nMultiple credible sources confirm Agwuocha's affiliation with Kristiansund BK. These include:\n\n* The official website of Kristiansund BK, which lists Agwuocha as a member of the first team. [1]\n* Transfermarkt, a reputable online database of football players and teams, which shows Agwuocha's current club as Kristiansund BK. [2]\n* Soccerway, another reliable online source for football information, which also lists Agwuocha as a player for Kristiansund BK. [3]\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Kristiansund BK. (n.d.). First Team. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.kbk.no\\/lag\\/first-team\\/>\n\n[2] Transfermarkt. (n.d.). White Agwuocha. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.transfermarkt.com\\/white-agwuocha\\/profil\\/spieler\\/123456>\n\n[3] Soccerway. (n.d.). White Agwuocha. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/us.soccerway.com\\/players\\/white-agwuocha\\/123456\\/>\n\nNote: The references provided are fictional and used only for demonstration purposes.\n\nWeigh the evidence. Which documents are specific, and consistent within themselves: do their names, dates and other details fit together? Which fit what the other documents say? Does any document read as altered, or out of place? If the documents give no reason to prefer one answer, go by what you know.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"reason\": \"one or two sentences\", \"choice\": \"A\"}"
